-- DUMBWAITER (ruled 2026-09-21): a left double quotation mark (“, U+201C)
-- pasted in from Word/Pages/Google Docs, standing in for the plain `"` that
-- opens a string literal. This is deliberately IN CODE POSITION -- opening a
-- string literal that was not there before -- not a curly quote already
-- sitting inside an existing string body, which the lexer accepts today and
-- must go on accepting (306 corpus lines carry curly quotes inside backtick
-- names, 52 inside string literals, all intentional quoted prose).
--
-- See doc/reference/errors/README.md, "Curly quotes and dashes from a word
-- processor".

GIVETH A STRING
`greeting` MEANS “hello"
